[54.762486, "i", "cat > FIX_SUMMARY.txt << 'EOF'\n=== RSYNC BACKUP ISSUE - RESOLVED ===\n\nPROBLEM:\n- Backup script running successfully (exit 0) but not transferring files\n- Source: 217 files, Dest: only 3 old files\n- Started after 2024-01-09 update\n\nROOT CAUSE:\n- exclude.lst was updated on 2024-01-09 with gitignore-style syntax:\n  *           (exclude everything)\n  !.gitkeep   (try to include .gitkeep)\n\n- rsync does NOT support '!' syntax for includes in --exclude-from files\n- This is a gitignore feature, not rsync\n- Result: rsync excluded ALL files, transferred 0 bytes\n\nFIX APPLIED:\n- Backed up broken file to exclude.lst.broken\n- Created new exclude.lst with proper rsync syntax\n- Re-ran sync: 220 files now in dest, 799KB transferred\n\nVERIFICATION:\n- Source and dest now match correctly\n- Sync working as expected\n\nNOTE: If you need to exclude specific patterns, use rsync syntax:\n  - Just list patterns to exclude (no '!' prefix)\n  - For complex include/exclude, use --include/--exclude flags in sync.sh\nEOF\n"]
